hern  nevada really got hit hard places like  perum  facing some dangerous driving conditions  these are telephone poles floating down  the road  come on come on buddy  unfortunately those flooded roadways  were just some of the ways the storms  have impacted that community madison  kimbrough continues  our team coverage from pahrump where  some say they haven't seen a downpour  like this  in years damage in pahrump  is extensive from heavy flooding to  uprooted trees like the one that you see  right here  in this neighborhood  [Applause]  it woke me up about 10 30 the thunder  lightning flashing all around  tom wilcox recalls the intense storm  from sunday into monday  afternoon he says the rainfall was so  loud he was worried his windows would  shatter  and as for the flooding this is video he  took of his street  he says he didn't dare leave the house  but saw some cars try to make it through  it was up about this far in our driveway  it's probably a foot deep in the road  yeah just flowing over at the pahrump  valley speedway owner chad broadhead  said it's been years since he's seen  this amount of flooding  and unfortunately the damage will cost  him and we just put a whole new surface  on this racetrack just a month ago  which cost a few thousand dollars to do  and now it's all washed out so we've got  to redo it  and as you can see behind me you can see  anywhere from 6 to 12 feet of water in  both our lower pit parking and  our racetrack so what's next for the  speedway broadhead says  at this point it's a waiting game we  cancel our races for a while  we start back in and do a complete  cleanup  we try to fix our buildings as for the  damage you can see the cleanup has begun  and the owner of this home says it could  have been much worse he's just happy  that his roof is still intact  reporting in pahrump madison kimbrough 8  news now  parts of henderson still cleaning up  from that micro burst that hit  thursday at arroyo grande park some of  the softball